        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017 EAACI and John Wiley and Sons A/S. Published by John Wiley and Sons Ltd.",
        "AbstractText": "Treatment with SQ (standardised quality) house dust mite sublingual tablet for 1 year resulted in a decreased probability of having an allergic rhinitis (AR) exacerbation day (from 11% [placebo] to 5% [SQ house dust mite sublingual tablet]) and an increased probability of having a mild AR day (from 16% [placebo] to 34% [SQ house dust mite sublingual tablet])."
